Rule 4 (If the input is a tuple, it should not be empty.)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len > 0
>>
Rule 5 (If the input is a tensor, its elements must be finite.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) > -1000000000.0 ∧ max(v_1) < 1000000000.0
>>
Rule 6 (If input is a tensor, its shape should be reasonable)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ndim(v_1) - 1 else 0] : shape(v_1, i) < 10000
